      "execution": {
        "output": "To find out how many gallons of milk Aunt May has left, we need to first calculate the total amount of milk she collected today. We can do this by adding the milk she got this morning (365 gallons) and this evening (380 gallons). \n\nTotal milk collected = 365 + 380 = 745 gallons\n\nNext, we subtract the amount of milk she sold (612 gallons) from the total milk collected. However, before doing that, we need to add the leftover milk from yesterday (15 gallons).\n\nTotal milk available for sale = Total milk collected - leftover milk\n= 745 - 15 \n= 730 gallons\n\nNow, we can subtract the amount of milk she sold from the total milk available for sale.\n\nMilk left over = Total milk available for sale - milk sold\n= 730 - 612 \n= 118 gallons\n\nSo, Aunt May has 118 gallons of milk left.",
